# Two categories of command that need no allowed-tools grant:
#  - named but never run: printed for the engineer, quoted as a defect, or a
#    line the skill writes into another file; the reason says so.
#  - run by the skill but deliberately not pre-approved (a grant would be too
#    wide or is forbidden by lint-skills): the reason starts with "prompts:"
#    and the harness asks each time.
# One row per command: <skill>|<command prefix>|<reason>. Keep the reason
# specific; lint-tools fails on a row that no longer matches anything.
api-versioning|make test-contracts|a target the skill adds to the Makefile
company-attribution|make check|the gate the skill adds headers-check to
license-compliance|make licenses|a target the skill adds to the Makefile
license-compliance|npm ci|named as a reproducible-build flag in the release notes
license-compliance|uv sync --frozen|named as a reproducible-build flag in the release notes
secrets|make env-check|a target the skill adds to the Makefile
doctor|make setup|run only inside a throwaway clone to reproduce, never in the user's clone
doctor|git update-index|a fix line printed for the engineer
doctor|npm install|named as the step that resets core.hooksPath, never run
gate-audit|git ls-files|an example of a gate pattern that passes on empty input
mcp-server|claude mcp add|a registration line printed for the user
learn|gh issue create|a command printed for the engineer to file the proposal, never run
postmortem|git log|output the caller pasted; the skill reads it, never runs it
release|npm i|a README install line the skill greps for
release|pnpm add|a README install line the skill greps for
release|go get|a README install line the skill greps for
workflow|git init|a next action named for the engineer
docs-drift|make test|a docs claim the skill checks against the recipe, never runs
# References and bodies that mention a command in prose, a rule or a recipe text.
flutter|flutter run|a guideline sentence on the build-define file, never run by the skill
flutter|flutter build|a guideline sentence on the build-define file, never run by the skill
flutter|flutter create|a review-checklist line about files it regenerates, never run
nextjs|pnpm dlx shadcn|a rule telling the engineer how to add a component, never run by the skill
react|pnpm dlx shadcn|a rule telling the engineer how to add a component, never run by the skill
react-native|npx expo install --fix|a rule naming the fix for an out-of-range dependency, never run
data-pipeline|dbt run|a guideline sentence on how models are run, never run by the skill
data-pipeline|dbt deps|a guideline sentence on package install, never run by the skill
data-pipeline|dbt source freshness|a guideline sentence on a freshness task, never run by the skill
data-pipeline|dbt docs generate|a guideline sentence on the docs artifact, never run by the skill
data-pipeline|airflow backfill create|a backfill command named for the engineer; backfills are run by the engineer
data-pipeline|uv lock|a rule that the lock file is regenerated, never run by the skill
python|uv lock|a rule that the lock file is regenerated, never run by the skill
python|alembic upgrade head|a test-setup sentence in the guidelines, never run by the skill
go|docker compose|a test-setup sentence in the guidelines, never run by the skill
go|go 1.21|the text of a go.mod directive in a review item, not a command
infra|terraform test|a review rule about test files, never run by the skill
database|diff A B|a verification recipe the scaffolds ship, named for the engineer
database|make migrate-verify|a target the scaffolds ship; the skill names it and never runs it
database|goose up-to|a migration step named in a rollback recipe for the engineer
database|alembic upgrade|a migration step named in a rollback recipe for the engineer
harness-setup|docker exec|a wrapper command the permission matcher follows, named as an example
llm-fine-tuning|make train-|a target the recipe adds to the Makefile
definition-of-done|pnpm exec vitest run|an example of the test command passed to red_proof.sh, the granted entry point
gate-audit|git add|the body of a pre-commit hook quoted as a defect, never run
merge-request|git add|a line printed for the engineer to commit the progress file
merge-request|git commit -m|a line printed for the engineer to commit the progress file
observability|docker compose -f observability/docker-compose.observability.yml up|the recipe text written into the observability-up target
openapi-spec|docker compose up -d --wait|a step of the CI job the skill writes, not run by the skill
openapi-spec|make migrate|a step of the CI job the skill writes, not run by the skill
release|pip install|a README install line the skill greps for
release|uv add|a README install line the skill greps for
harness-setup|git -C|prompts: the skill reads the kit remote URL; lint-skills forbids a git -C grant, so the harness asks
test-run|DATABASE_URL=... go test|prompts: run by the skill; an env-prefix grant would also match a smuggled command, so the harness asks
test-run|PLAYWRIGHT_JSON_OUTPUT_NAME=|prompts: run by the skill; an env-prefix grant would also match a smuggled command, so the harness asks
test-run|DATABASE_URL=... uv run pytest|prompts: run by the skill; an env-prefix grant would also match a smuggled command, so the harness asks
spike|rm -r .scratch/spike-|prompts: run by the skill to delete the throwaway; a glob grant on rm is too wide, so the harness asks
